AI-Assisted Police Report Lodging
Home Team Science & Technology Agency (HTX) × Singapore Police Force

Project Overview
SPF's existing online report lodging system required citizens to fill in a standardised form regardless of the type of incident they were reporting. While the system captured basic information, it provided no guidance on what level of detail was needed, resulting in reports that were frequently incomplete or ambiguous. Investigation officers routinely had to follow up with complainants to clarify missing information, reducing their capacity for higher-priority work.

I was brought in to design R-COP (Report Lodging Co-Pilot): an AI-assisted chatbot that guides citizens through the report lodging process conversationally, using a curated question set adapted from existing SPF investigation workflows. R-COP surfaces case-type-specific follow-up questions based on what the citizen has described, prompting for the details officers need for their case investigation. Once the conversation is complete, the system generates a structured report summary for the citizen to review and confirm before submitting.
